/given-names></name><name><surname>Musagara</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1991</year><article-title>Dynamics of spread of HIV-I infection in a rural district of Uganda.</article-title><source>Bmj</source><volume>303</volume><fpage>1303</fpage><lpage>1306</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1747672</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004145-UgandaMOH1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>Uganda-MOH</collab><year>2006</year><source>Uganda Ministry of Health: Uganda HIV/AIDS Sero-behavioural Survey 2004&#x02013;2005</source><publisher-loc>Kampala</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Uganda Ministry of Health and ORC Macro Calverton, Maryland, USA</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004145-Mermin1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mermin</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Musinguzi</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Opio</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirungi</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekwaru</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Risk factors for recent HIV infection in Uganda.</article-title><source>Jama</source><volume>300</volume><fpage>540</fpage><lpage>549</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18677026</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004145-UNAIDS1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><collab>UNAIDS</collab><year>2006</year><article-title>UNAIDS Reference Group on estimates, modelling and projections&#x02013;statement on the use of the BED assay for the estimation of HIV-1 incidence for surveillance or epidemic monitoring.</article-title><source>Wkly Epidemiol Rec</source><volume>81</volume><fpage>40</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16671237</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004145-UBOS1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>UBOS</collab><year>2001</year><comment>Uganda Bureau of Statistics (UBOS): Population and Housing Census 2000 Report</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004145-Eller1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eller</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Eller</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ouma</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kataaha</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Bagaya</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Large-scale human immunodeficiency virus rapid test evaluation in a low-prevalence ugandan blood bank population.</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><volume>45</volume><fpage>3281</fpage><lpage>3285</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17699650</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004145-Arroyo2"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Arroyo</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoelscher</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanders-Buell</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Herbinger</surname><given-names>KH</given-names></name><name><surname>Samky</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>HIV type 1 subtypes among blood donors in the Mbeya region of southwest Tanzania.</article-title><source>AIDS Res Hum Retroviruses</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>895</fpage><lpage>901</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15320994</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004145-Hoelscher1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoelscher</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Dowling</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name><name><surname>Sander