wari</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>HU</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Incidence of HIV-1 infection in adults and socio-demographic characteristics of seroconverters in a rural population in Uganda: 1990&#x02013;1994.</article-title><source>Int J Epidemiol</source><volume>25</volume><fpage>1077</fpage><lpage>1082</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8921497</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004145-Mbulaiteye1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mbulaiteye</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mahe</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Whitworth</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruberantwari</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakiyingi</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Declining HIV-1 incidence and associated prevalence over 10 years in a rural population in south-west Uganda: a cohort study.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>360</volume><fpage>41</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12114040</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004145-Gray1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gray</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Kigozi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Serwadda</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Makumbi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Watya</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Male circumcision for HIV prevention in men in Rakai, Uganda: a randomised trial.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>369</volume><fpage>657</fpage><lpage>666</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">173